// plume-starter.js  v2.0
//
// The Quick add starter list (Ingredients -> Settings -> Quick add), meant
// to be comprehensive enough to start a library from, for Heide now and for
// the sellable version later. Loaded as a plain script, like
// plume-sapdata.js. 261 ingredients in 18 types.
//
// SHAPE: { types: [names in display order], items: [ingredient, ...] }.
// Each item is an ingredient record plus 'type', and 'aka' (former names from
// the merge, used by search and the in-library check; neither is stored on
// the ingredient). Add an ingredient by adding
// an item with one of the listed types; a test fails on an unknown type.
//
// HISTORY (2026-10-16). Built from two sources: Plume's own curated starter
// list and the Formula Botanica Ingredients Directory (fb_ingredients.json,
// which used to arrive through a separate import button, since removed).
// Then reorganized for a general audience, at Heide's direction:
//   - by ingredient TYPE, not by the batch it was added in (the old tabs
//     included 'Your Ingredients', her purchase history);
//   - one entry per ingredient: '(organic)' and '(soap grade)' purchasing
//     variants and repeats folded together, while real grades stay apart
//     (virgin vs 76-degree coconut, regular vs high-oleic sunflower, the two
//     hyaluronic acid weights, tea-seed vs japonica camellia);
//   - the directory's general-information paragraphs REMOVED. They are
//     Formula Botanica's prose and do not belong in a product sold to others.
//     Short factual fields stay (INCI, use range, phase, absorption, melting
//     point, stability, scent, colour). Heide's own library keeps whatever
//     text it already has; this file only affects what Quick add offers.
//
// NO SAP NUMBERS LIVE HERE. Quick add looks each oil up in plume-sapdata.js
// by name as it is added: SoapCalc's value, or none if SoapCalc lacks the
// oil or it is unknown on purpose. A fatty acid profile here is a fallback;
// the reference's profile wins.
